{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<h2>Install the CLI</h2>
<pre><code>go install github.com/donseba/go-clue@latest</code></pre>

<h2>Install the experimental generator</h2>
<p>Only install this when you want to use <code>@gen</code> helper namespaces.</p>
<pre><code>go install github.com/donseba/go-clue/cmd/go-clue-exp-gen@latest</code></pre>

<h2>Install an editor package</h2>
<table class="table">
    <thead><tr><th>Editor</th><th>Release asset</th><th>Needs</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>GoLand</td><td><code>go-clue-goland-plugin-*.zip</code></td><td>GoLand 2025.3 or newer. Install with Settings &gt; Plugins &gt; Install Plugin from Disk.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>VS Code</td><td><code>go-clue-vscode-*.vsix</code></td><td>VS Code 1.90 or newer. Install with Extensions: Install from VSIX.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sublime Text</td><td><code>go-clue-sublime-*.sublime-package</code></td><td>The LSP package from Package Control.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vim</td><td><code>go-clue-vim-*.zip</code></td><td>Vim 8.2 or newer with <code>prabirshrestha/vim-lsp</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Neovim</td><td><code>go-clue-neovim-*.zip</code></td><td>Neovim 0.10 or newer.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Each editor has a README with its install steps in the <a href="https://github.com/donseba/go-clue/tree/main/ide">ide folder</a> of the repository.</p>

<h2>No project files required</h2>
<p>The editor integrations start <code>go-clue lsp</code>. The language server uses the nearest <code>go.mod</code> above each template and scans that module in memory, and does not require a <code>.go-clue</code> folder. It still starts in a folder with no <code>go.mod</code>; templates there get no Go types.</p>

<h2>Optional index file</h2>
<p><code>.go-clue/index.json</code> is only needed when you explicitly want a generated artifact for CI, debugging, or other tools.</p>
<pre><code>go-clue index -o .go-clue/index.json .</code></pre>
</article>
